// The connector's own schedule.
//
// Only three of the connector's own, and the shortness is the point: the data-origins runtime
// (component/datasync) already owns inbound dispatch, the reconciliation
// runner and the outbox drain, and it drives them from
// dsl/platform/automations.memql for EVERY connector. What is left here
// is what is Shopify's alone, and, last, the store statistics rollup, which
// reads this overlay's store statistics queries.

/// Reconcile every store's webhook subscriptions daily.
///
/// Shopify retries a failed delivery eight times over four hours and then
/// DELETES the subscription. A deployment that was unreachable for an
/// afternoon comes back with its webhooks silently gone -- the mirror
/// simply stops changing, and nothing anywhere says so. This is what
/// brings them back, and the store's health is where an operator sees
/// that it happened.
///
/// Not the runtime's job: EnsureSubscriptions is a contract verb, but
/// nothing generic can know how often a given origin forgets its
/// subscribers.
@trigger(schedule="0 15 3 * * *")
automation reconcileShopifySubscriptions {
  ensure := builtin shopifyEnsureSubscriptions()
}

/// Watch every store's verdict every five minutes: record it on the store, and tell the store's
/// owner once when it has needed attention for the alert wait and once when it is recording again.
/// single: a pass that outlasts five minutes is not overlapped by the next one in this process.
@trigger(schedule="0 */5 * * * *")
@mode(single)
automation watchShopifyStores {
  watch := builtin shopifyWatchStores()
}

/// Run the privacy jobs that are due, hourly: a request whose hold has
/// elapsed, the second pass of an erasure an hour after its first, and a job
/// that failed, which is run again at every run until it is done.
///
/// Hourly rather than on delivery, because both windows are measured in
/// days -- customers/redact has thirty and shop/redact a 48-hour hold --
/// and running on receipt would override a merchant's own grace period.
/// At minute 7 and not on a multiple of five, because the continuing backfill
/// pass begins every five minutes, and a run that began with one would land
/// its scrub and its restart of the store's backfills while a page was being
/// applied.
/// single: a run takes jobs for twenty minutes and finishes the one it is on,
/// and a run that outlasts the hour is not overlapped by the next.
@trigger(schedule="0 7 * * * *")
@mode(single)
automation runShopifyComplianceJobs {
  run := builtin shopifyRunComplianceJobs()
}

/// Keep every store's statistics (the 2026-11-11 store statistics design): every minute on the
/// cron leader, at second 15, so it does not start in the same second as the other rollups.
///
/// THE WORK IS A BUILTIN, builtin storeStatisticsRollup in component/storestats, because its output
/// is no concept: side tables of facts the statistics read sums with SQL. It reads the stores and
/// their mirror rows through the engine from Go, and its one step answers counts, so no row of a
/// store's mirror is kept in this automation's journal.
///
/// A MAINTENANCE automation (component/auth/maintenance_actor.go): the builtin admits this
/// automation's maintenance principal and no other caller, so the default reader actor would be
/// refused on every run.
@trigger(schedule="15 * * * * *")
automation storeStatisticsRollupSweep {
  roll := builtin storeStatisticsRollup()
}

/// Check every store's statistics against its mirror (the 2026-11-11 store statistics design): every
/// hour on the cron leader, at minute 40, where no other hourly sweep begins. Each run carries every
/// caught-up store's pass on, comparing each fact with what its mirrored row gives now by version and
/// by content -- the walk trusts versions, and a customer's erasure rewrites rows in place where no
/// walk looks -- writing again what differs and, at the end of a pass, deleting the facts no row
/// answers for.
///
/// THE WORK IS A BUILTIN, builtin storeStatisticsCheck in component/storestats, for the rollup's
/// reasons: it reads the mirror rows from Go and its one step answers counts, so no row of a store's
/// mirror is kept in this automation's journal.
///
/// A MAINTENANCE automation (component/auth/maintenance_actor.go): the builtin admits this
/// automation's maintenance principal and no other caller.
@trigger(schedule="0 40 * * * *")
automation storeStatisticsCheckSweep {
  check := builtin storeStatisticsCheck()
}
